{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>As he charged them.</b> He said to them: take care with my bier that none of the sons of the Canaanite women may touch it, and you yourselves shall carry it in this manner: Yehudah, Yissachar, and Zevulun from the east; Reuven, Shimon, and Gad from the south; Ephraim, Menasheh, and Binyamin from the west; Dan, Asher, and Naphtali from the north. Yoseif shall not carry, because he is a king. Levi shall not carry, because he is destined to carry the Ark of the Holy One, blessed be He, and it is not fitting that he should carry the bier of a dead man. If you carry my bier according to my charge, the Holy One, blessed be He, is destined to cause divisions [degel] to rest upon you in the wilderness. And this is what our Rabbis of blessed memory said: ״וישאו אותו בניו״ — 'and his sons carried him' — and not his sons' sons."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:21:56.358889061Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}